 "reports_individuals_with_tnfaip3_variant": true,
 "relevance_note": "A 288-patient pediatric AID cohort that describes two HA20 patients individually only by their TNFAIP3 variants: \"p.R271X of the TNFAIP3 gene in one patient and p.R45X in the other one\".",
 "method_note": "Read by hand; no script transcribed tables. Only the two HA20 patients are in scope; the other 77 diagnosed and 209 undiagnosed patients (cohort 288) get no rows. The two people are labelled unnamed person 1 (p.R271X) and unnamed person 2 (p.R45X), in order of mention in the only sentence that separates them individually. The paper never links the per-patient facts across sentences: 'One patient was diagnosed as Behçet disease previously and the other one was diagnosed with undifferentiated connective tissue disease' and 'Hashimoto′s thyroiditis was also found in one patient' cannot be tied to either variant, so prior diagnoses and thyroiditis are left not reported for both. Table 2 (A20 deficiency row) gives only group values: age at onset median 4 (range 0–8), clinical findings list (fever, rash, arthralgia, mucosal ulcers, bowel inflammation, CTD) and variants 'p.R45X, p.R271X' in one cell; none assigned to a person (group lists without names). Sex female for both from the group ratio 0:2 (male:female) of the named n = 2 group. Table 2 'Inheritance AD' is the disease's mode of inheritance, not the variants' origin; inheritance and zygosity left not reported. Variant type not derived from the 'X' notation. Oral ulcer row from 'both suffered from recurrent oral ulcer' (named group of the two HA20 patients), recorded as inferred from group statement. Ethnicity ('Chinese') and consanguinity ('There was no consanguinity in these children') come from statements about the whole cohort; treatment from 'HA20 patients ... anti-TNF-α therapies'. 'They all had persistently or intermittently elevated inflammation indices' is in Patient Selection (study inclusion criteria), so not used for the inflammatory-marker checklist item. cites_prior_report_of_same_patients is true because the NLRP12 patients were reported earlier (ref 12); nothing says the HA20 patients were. References 25, 26 are cited for the variants' pathogenicity, not as earlier reports of these patients. is_proband left null (cohort; no proband named). No contradictions found.",
